{"entity": "Yesus", "type": "person", "description": "Yesus is a central figure presented as the Son of God and the ultimate revelation of God, sent into the world to demonstrate God's perfect character and to provide salvation. His life and atoning death are considered key to understanding God's love and the Father. Yesus is seen as the answer to knowing God and deepening a relationship with Him, offering a generous exchange and urging repentance.\n\nHe is depicted as the Savior and Redeemer, offering solutions and describing the spiritual condition of believers. Yesus overcame sin and its punishment, and His teachings emphasize abiding in Him, obeying Him, and remaining in His love. He is also mentioned in the context of correcting misconceptions about Allah. His role is to offer salvation and foster a close relationship with humanity."}
{"entity": "Adam", "type": "person", "description": "Adam is the first human, into whom God breathed the breath of life."}
{"entity": "Manusia Pertama", "type": "creature", "description": "The first human was formed by God from the dust of the ground and given the breath of life."}
{"entity": "Ellen G. White", "type": "person", "description": "Ellen G. White is an author who wrote about the importance of remaining connected to Christ and receiving the Holy Spirit daily.<SEP>Ellen G. White is an author whose writings, such as \"Membina Kehidupan Abadi\" and \"Testimonies,\" provide insights into God's character and His relationship with humanity.<SEP>Ellen G. White is an author who wrote \"Testimonies for the Church\" and \"Sejarah Para Nabi,\" expanding on Lucifer's deception and Allah's character.<SEP>Ellen G. White is cited regarding the diversity and richness of the four Gospels in conveying the knowledge of Jesus.<SEP>Ellen G. White is an author who wrote about the experiences of the Gospel writers and the nature of God's love."}
{"entity": "The Desire of Ages", "type": "content", "description": "This is a book by Ellen G. White that discusses remaining in Christ and receiving the Holy Spirit."}
{"entity": "1 Petrus 1:13-16", "type": "content", "description": "1 Petrus 1:13-16 is a biblical passage that, along with others, calls God's people to live holy lives."}
{"entity": "Allah", "type": "person", "description": "Allah is described as the one true God, the central divine entity who is the foundation of a strong relationship with believers. His character is characterized by glory, mercy, compassion, truth, holiness, goodness, and love. Allah is also portrayed as omniscient, omnipotent, and sovereign over all creation, being transcendent and beyond human understanding, yet in control of everything. He is the true Creator and the ultimate object of worship and trust.\n\nThe descriptions highlight Allah's desire for closeness with humanity, noting that He interacts with people in different ways across time and invites them into a covenant relationship. Believers are called to obey His commands as an act of love, recognizing that Allah Himself first loved humanity. While Allah is infinitely greater than human comprehension, He is worthy of praise and is presented as the Father who loves and the divine being with whom humans have a relationship. Some descriptions also mention alternative names like Elohim and Yahweh, which describe different aspects of His being. Furthermore, Allah is said to have a clear and beautiful image that is important for deepening one's relationship with Him."}
